From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:24:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 42/99] v8: e2k: do not end the scheduling window where nothing
 counts instructions

A memory access asked for its position for the trap handler, which
exists only with WebAssembly: every load and store of TurboFan code
started a window. BlockTrampolinePoolScope, which marks sequences whose
instructions are counted, also stood (from loong64, for the trampoline
pool that is not there) in branches without a link, compares, overflow
checks, conversions, frame entry, register calls and jumps, and around
every branch of the code generator: removed where the instructions are
not counted. StackOverflowCheck branches are rare.
